7. Complexity

Finish with:

"The average time complexity is O(n log n), because the array is generally divided into balanced parts. The worst case is O(n²), 
which can happen when the pivot repeatedly becomes the smallest or largest element.
The space complexity is O(log n) on average because of the recursion stack, and O(n) in the worst case."
