🔥 Full answer to memorize

If the interviewer says "Explain your Merge Sort code", say:

"Merge Sort is a Divide and Conquer algorithm. First, I divide the array into two halves recursively until each part contains one element. Then I merge the two sorted halves. During merging, I use two pointers, one for each half, and compare their elements. I put the smaller element into a temporary array and move that pointer forward. If one half finishes, I copy the remaining elements from the other half. Finally, I copy the temporary array back to the original array. The time complexity is O(n log n) and the space complexity is O(n)."

🧠 One-line memory trick

mergeSort() = Divide

merge() = Compare + Combine

Overall:

Divide → Left recursion → Right recursion → Merge

That's the explanation I'd recommend giving in your Infosys interview—simple, clear, and enough to show that you actually understand the code rather than memorized it.
